# Website submodule (`website/`)

The marketing site at `website/` is a **git submodule** pointing at https://github.com/phoenix-language/website. It has its own Git history, PRs, issues, and deployment — not part of the compiler workspace crates.

## Clone and init

New clones must include submodules:

```bash
git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/phoenix-language/phoenix.git
```

Existing clones:

```bash
git submodule update --init --recursive
```

An empty or missing `website/` directory means submodules were not initialized.

## Local development

- Nested Justfile: `website/justfile`
- From repo root: `just website dev`, `just website open`, `just website --list`
- Do **not** add website build/lint to `just pre-commit` unless explicitly requested — compiler CI stays Rust-only.

## Editing the website

Submodules often checkout a detached HEAD. Before new work:

```bash
cd website
git checkout main
```

Make changes, then commit **inside the submodule first**:

```bash
cd website
git add .
git commit -m "Describe website change"
git push origin main
```

Then bump the submodule pointer in the parent phoenix repo:

```bash
cd ..
git add website
git commit -m "[infra]: bump website submodule"
```

## Rules for agents

1. **Never** commit website source files (HTML, CSS, JS, assets) only in the phoenix parent repo — they live in the submodule remote.
2. **Always** commit and push website changes from inside `website/` before updating the parent pointer.
3. Parent-repo commits that only change the submodule SHA use prefix `[infra]:` (e.g. `[infra]: bump website submodule`, `[infra]: add website git submodule`).
4. When cloning or CI needs the site tree, ensure `git submodule update --init --recursive` runs.
5. Website stack is currently static HTML (`index.html`, `style.css`, `scripts.js`); no pnpm/cargo in `website/` until migrated.
